  "modelling_notes": [
    "Finland source event percentages overlap; they are converted to relative weights, sex/age-shaped, normalized within the 80% with a reported recent life event, and retain a 20% unresolved bucket.",
    "Canada age 50-64/65-74/75+ uses the Alberta study. Published age-specific physical/mental/financial percentages are retained within the known-stressor distribution; the residual is allocated in the sex-specific proportions of the other Alberta stressor categories. The published 55-64 cell is used as the 50-64 gameplay bracket.",
    "Canadian age groups below 50 use Montreal sex-specific coroner variables as relative anchors. Because those variables are overlapping and not age-cross-tabulated, age shaping is explicitly model-derived and the cell provenance says so.",
    "FI_CA_REFERENCE is an equal 50/50 average of the already-normalized Finnish and Canadian probabilities, not population-weighted. It is intended only as a transparent fallback for future countries/cells without native data."
  ]
